% Part III: the predicates the LLM may define (Chapter 12).
% `assert_clause` adds clauses, never declarations, so
% every predicate a generated rule defines is declared
% here first. The declaration is the contract.
accumulate derived.

% ANCHOR: open
pred knows o:person, o:person.
% ANCHOR_END: open

% A rule the LLM wrote is explained as one step.
direct (knows _ _) "learned rule".

% ANCHOR: question
% A holder for LLM-written queries: the agent type-checks
% `question :- Query.` before it runs Query.
pred question.
% ANCHOR_END: question
